WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.470
Tomorrow is the long-awaited
Christmas Eve!

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.070
In order to confess
my love to Takuto,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.630
I've worked hard night after night
to knit a scarf for him!

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.830
But...but...but...

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.570
Why?!

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:15.400
I'm not done yet!

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.600
Mitsuki!

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:19.500
Please! Help me so I can
finish it in time!

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.730
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.470
Got that?

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:29.530
Yes.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.070
What am I going to do?

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.530
We forgot about your grandmother.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:10.370
We were being careless.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.070
We were on cloud nine after
the Best New Singer Award.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.870
And it's not like I can butt in...

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.630
Well, you at least have a passport.
It could have been worse.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.770
That's not the problem.
We have to persuade her grandmother.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.130
That's right.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:29.600
I know!

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:35.070
Meroko, you transform into Mitsuki
and stay at home.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:35.770
What?!

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.870
So you mean I have to
stay home alone?

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.970
You've got it.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.970
Takuto, do you really intend to go
and leave me?!

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.670
Huh?

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.530
- You're so mean!
- Ouch! Oww!

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.470
- That's outrageous! You've gone too far!
- Ouch, I get it!

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.730
What do you wanna do, Mitsuki?
Should we ask Meroko to do that?

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:55.830
No.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:59.000
I want to go tell Grandma about
going to America.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:05.600
I once lied to Grandma and went
to a sleepover.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.170
That time, I felt like I had lied
to Grandma's feelings as well.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.130
That's why this time
I want to tell her properly.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:22.500
Yes.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:27.870
About that, I've gathered the information
so please come to the hospital.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:36.270
So this is that new
treatment method?

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:41.530
Yes. If we continue the current treatment
and do the operation,

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:45.100
there's a possibility she
would lose her voice,

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.930
but with this treatment method
Dr. Lon Herberd wrote about,

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.800
there is no worry of that.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:51.670
And?

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:56.270
I contacted that doctor,
and we came to an agreement.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.170
Then, Dr. Wakaoji...

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.070
Yes.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.700
Yay! Then I'm sure
your grandmother will okay it!

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.170
What do you mean?

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.730
That Dr. What's-His-Name will
examine Mitsuki's throat!

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.430
What?

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:16.130
If we tell her that, your grandmother will
understand and let you go to America.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.200
Really?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:18.930
Yep.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.000
I'll come to
your house tomorrow,

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.430
and we'll talk to your grandmother
about everything, okay?

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:25.630
Yes!

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:42.470
So, I contacted the doctor and he'd like to
examine the condition of Mitsuki's illness.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:48.500
Then he'll determine whether this
treatment method can be used on Mitsuki.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.470
So...

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.370
You're saying you'd like to take
Mitsuki to America?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:54.430
Yes.

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.230
It's quite sudden isn't it?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.130
Grandma...

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.900
Doctors in Japan can't do
that medical treatment?

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.630
Unfortunately, no doctors in Japan
have attempted this treatment yet.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.100
I thought that I'd study it on this trip
so that I can be of help in the future.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:18.430
DEPARTURE FROM
CONVENTIONAL APPROACH
FOR THROAT DISEASE TREATMENT

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.870
I'm against it.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.570
What?!

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.700
Why, Grandma?

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.200
I don't understand that medical
treatment very well yet.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:32.630
No matter how many times
you explain that it's "good,"

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:35.300
I won't allow something I don't understand
for my beloved granddaughter.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.700
However, if you actually
meet the doctor...

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.370
I understand what you're saying.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:44.470
But to go to America
for only that reason.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:49.530
Can't we wait until he has
the opportunity to come to Japan?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.570
Well...

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.730
Mitsuki is a child with a weak body.

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:56.770
I can't agree to taking that child
around America.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:00.130
My number one concern is
this child's body.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.830
Is that wrong?

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.630
Mrs. Koyama, you're right
to be concerned, but...

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:08.800
Mitsuki, you shouldn't
just jump at new things

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:11.430
because you've heard
that they're good.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.070
But Mrs. Koyama!

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:17.470
What would you do if something
happened while she was in America?

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.170
Would you take responsibility?

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.370
Grandma!

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.130
You be quiet.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.700
No! Please!
Grandma, please understand.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:30.530
With this medical treatment
I won't lose my voice!

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.370
I'll be able to keep doing what
I love to do... sing!

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:37.670
Mitsuki!

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:44.170
You...can't possibly still have
an interest in music, can you?!

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.330
Well?!

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:48.700
Mitsuki...

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.230
Mitsuki!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.500
I'm a singer...

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.570
I mean, I want to be a singer!

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:58.800
Grandma!

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:02.170
I want you to hear
my song, Grandma!

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:04.830
That's why I don't want
to lose my voice!

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.770
Dr. Wakaoji,
what is this all about?

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:13.470
It's just like Mitsuki said.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:19.470
The two of you were
making a fool of me.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:20.770
That's wrong!

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.470
That's enough! I don't want
to hear anything else!

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.070
Mrs. Koyama!

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:29.170
Grandma, please!
Please let me go to America!

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.200
I absolutely will not allow it.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.970
Umm... Ma'am, Mitsuki is...

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.630
How dare you!
It's disgraceful to eavesdrop!

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:42.070
Y-Yes! I'm sorry!

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.370
Keep your spirits up.
I'll try asking her again tomorrow.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:04.400
Okay...

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.530
We'll make sure that you can go.
So don't worry.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:09.770
Yes.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.400
The operation...

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:13.570
Is it in there?

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.800
THINGS THAY MAY INTERRUPT FATE
THERE ARE NO NEW MESSAGES
No, it looks like it's okay.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:17.770
I see.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:20.970
What is it?

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.270
We're in an unfortunate business.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.200
Yeah.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.600
Grandma, please listen to me.

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.030
I'm coming in.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.130
I'm sorry that I've
kept quiet about music.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:56.530
Of course,
I've known that you are against it.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.570
But I really want to be a singer.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:06.900
I believe that you are concerned
that my body is weak.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:11.100
But please let me go to America.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.570
I can't do that.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:18.370
Why? Why, Grandma?

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:22.530
Is it because I didn't tell you
about my music?

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.900
Do you hate music that much?

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:29.230
Even though my mother and
I like music this much?

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:35.200
Why? Grandma, why don't you
understand my feelings at all?

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:40.500
I'm sure that my mother ran away from
home because you're like that, Grandma!

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.500
Grandma...

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.030
Grandma...

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.700
Grandma, I hate you!

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:51.030
Mitsuki!

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.570
<i>Mother, I hate you!</i>

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.530
What are you doing?

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:12.770
Packing to go to America.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.730
What? But you still...

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.670
Hey, my life goes until spring
of next year, right?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:24.900
Then...

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.930
I want to at least sing until then.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.400
And I'm going to America,
no matter what.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.700
Didn't Wakaoji say that he's going
to talk to her again?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.030
It won't work! Grandma won't
go back on what she said.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.670
On top of that,
this might be my last chance.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.030
Hey, where are you going?

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:56.500
To Ms. Oshige's...

00:10:56.730 --> 00:11:00.570
Well, shouldn't you
at least tell Ms. Tanaka?

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:05.270
Ms. Koyama, here's your mail!

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.370
Oh...thank you.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.030
It's addressed to Grandma...

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:14.830
MRS. FUZUKI KOYAMA
HIMEKI MUSIC ACADEMY
A music school?!

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:15.530
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.700
I'd love to see you.
It's been so long.

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:24.130
Grandma graduated
from a music school?!

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:49.570
I wonder if it's this way.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:52.770
Hey, what's the point of doing this?

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:56.300
Grandma went to a music school!

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.670
The person who
sent this postcard

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:01.330
probably knows the reason
why she started hating music.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:37.770
Have you been waiting?

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:42.830
I'm sorry, the lesson went
a little bit long.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:48.970
I'm deeply touched that Fuzuki's
granddaughter would come all this way.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.070
I'm sorry to trouble you.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.070
Don't worry about it.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:55.630
Oh, is tea okay with you?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.330
Oh... Yes, thank you.

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.500
Wow, it smells good.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:03.130
It's rose tea.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.630
And here are some cookies.
I just baked them.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:09.670
Please have some,
if you'd like.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.400
Thank you.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.630
It would have been nice if this kind of
person were her grandmother.

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:28.330
Shh...

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:37.300
Is something wrong?

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:39.230
Oh no...

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:48.100
So, Fuzuki really didn't
tell you anything, did she?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.000
No.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:56.070
Fuzuki and I were childhood friends.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.930
We really liked music.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:04.500
Fuzuki would often play
the piano while I would sing.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:09.530
And then we both
entered music school.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:16.330
Fuzuki got engaged to someone
she met at the school.

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.630
And my, how she glowed so brightly.

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:21.530
Engaged?

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.370
Yes.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:24.870
But then...

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:29.600
<i>It's no good!</i>
<i>And the competition is so soon!</i>

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:34.700
<i>You'll exhaust yourself</i>
<i>if you practice too much like that.</i>

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:36.400
<i>You have to take</i>
<i>a little break.</i>

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:38.930
<i>I don't care about that.</i>

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:44.530
<i>If I can't win this competition,</i>
<i>I'll never make it as a pianist in this world.</i>

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:45.500
<i>But—</i>

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:50.870
<i>Shut up! It's different for you because</i>
<i>music is just a hobby!</i>

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.430
<i>Don't bother me.</i>

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:00.900
As a result,
their feelings drifted apart.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:04.700
And he went abroad on his own.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:07.330
He left my grandmother?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:11.700
Yes... He chose
music over Fuzuki.

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:17.830
She debated whether or not
she should go with her fiancé,

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:21.630
but in the end, she made up her mind
to part from her fiancé and from music.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.400
She said that it was painful
to be exposed to music.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:30.500
But Fuzuki said that
she made the right decision.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:35.970
She said music is a demon that confuses
people's feeling and makes them unhappy.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:37.100
No way!

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.170
And then, after a while,
she contacted me.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.030
She said that she'd had
an arranged marriage.

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:51.270
And that she had been
blessed with a cute girl.

00:15:52.270 --> 00:15:54.970
That must be my mother.

00:15:56.570 --> 00:16:00.430
Back then, she would sometimes
come to this house to chat.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.930
She would bring
her young Hazuki with her.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:10.030
But since the young lady passed away,
she's been out of touch.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:16.270
It's been a while since then, so I started
wondering how she's doing now,

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:18.830
and I took it upon myself to send
a postcard for the class reunion.

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:20.370
Oh, I see.

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.870
But to have a lovely
granddaughter like you...

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.930
I'm sure that she's
very happy now.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.170
I'm glad.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:37.800
Today, I played very well,
and my teacher complimented me!

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:39.730
That's great!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:40.630
Yeah!

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.030
<i>When I first met Grandma...</i>

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.100
<i>the cherry blossoms</i>
<i>were in full bloom.</i>

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:54.530
<i>When I saw Grandma's frowning face,</i>
<i>I thought I wasn't really welcome.</i>

00:16:56.470 --> 00:17:00.470
<i>But back then,</i>
<i>Grandma was still suffering.</i>

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.000
What are you going to do?

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:12.730
What should I do?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.030
Can you persuade
your grandmother?

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.700
I don't think I can.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:23.070
So why are you
standing around here?

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.100
When I heard Grandma's story, I...

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:27.470
You're going home?

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:33.030
But if you return now,
she might lock you in.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.300
Is that okay with you?

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:40.770
Was I a bad girl for
making Grandma sad?

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:42.470
Mitsuki...

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:46.900
I cause her a lot of worry to begin with,
what with my weak body.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:49.170
But then to say that I want to be
a singer on top of that...

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:55.970
I'm sure that she hates even
hearing the word "music."

00:17:58.970 --> 00:17:59.970
Ma'am!

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:03.870
What is it?

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.400
Umm... Mitsuki is...

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.130
Mitsuki isn't here!

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.330
When I came to call her for dinner,
she was gone.

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:15.230
Almost all her things
are gone,

00:18:15.270 --> 00:18:18.100
and her beloved music box is
nowhere to be found.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.170
Could it be...
that she's run away?

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:26.170
<i>If you don't accept me,</i>
<i>Mother, then I'll move out!</i>

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.670
<i>Mother, I hate you!</i>

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:29.600
<i>Hazuki!</i>

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:34.630
<i>My beloved daughter, who means</i>
<i>more to me than anything.</i>

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:35.930
<i>And...</i>

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:41.330
<i>Thank you for taking me in.</i>
<i>My name is Mitsuki.</i>

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:45.000
<i>The child that was born in</i>
<i>exchange for that girl's life.</i>

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:49.670
<i>The child of the man</i>
<i>who stole Hazuki.</i>

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:52.270
<i>What should I say?</i>

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.800
<i>How should I speak to her?</i>

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:03.770
<i>But this time,</i>
<i>I have to protect her.</i>

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:10.800
You're not a bad girl.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:18.400
You never stopped wanting
your grandmother to like music.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:19.470
Am I wrong?

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:23.200
That shows that you care
about your grandmother.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:25.670
But...

00:19:26.400 --> 00:19:29.270
Well, can you tell her everything
about the length of your life?

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:30.200
What?

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.470
Takuto!
Why would you say that?!

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.370
If I tell her that,
Grandma will be sad.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:40.630
But if you don't, your grandmother won't
understand your feelings at all.

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.300
That's true, but...

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:47.430
I understand why your grandmother
came to hate music.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:52.500
But you have a reason why
you have to sing, don't you?

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.530
Takuto...

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:59.400
Why do you sing songs?

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:07.570
Tanaka! Contact every place
you can think of!

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:08.500
Yes!

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.800
Mitsuki!

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:14.230
Grandma...

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:18.300
Mitsuki! What a relief.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:21.530
What are you doing?
Hurry up and come in!

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:23.230
Grandma.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.370
What is it?

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:27.730
I'm going to America.

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:34.170
Even if you don't approve,
I want to go to America.

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:39.800
You're going to leave me too?

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:43.830
I'm sorry. I don't think
that you'll understand.

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:48.500
But Grandma, I love you.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.570
That wasn't true
when I said I hate you.

00:20:51.170 --> 00:20:52.770
Please just understand that.

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:58.030
Please listen to my songs someday!

00:20:59.100 --> 00:21:00.100
I'm sorry!

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.630
Mitsuki! Mitsuki—

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:05.500
Ma'am!

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.530
Ma'am, are you injured?!

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:09.470
Ma'am...

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.730
It's always the same.

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:23.900
It's always the things I hold dear
that pull away from my hands.

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:08.300
We're here in America!

00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:10.430
Hey Takuto,
where do you want to go?!

00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.670
You're completely
in sightseeing mode.

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:14.630
Do you understand,
you and I didn't come to play.

00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:15.870
You're so annoying!

00:23:15.970 --> 00:23:17.470
If you wanna talk
about being excited,

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:21.300
I'm not all that different from
that girl in full-on love mode with Eichi!

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:23.130
Once again,
you're taking her side!

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:25.400
It's so frustrating!

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:26.830
Stupid! Stop it, Meroko!

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:28.330
It's not like that!

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:32.870
Next time on Full Moon:
"Across the Pacific."

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:34.200
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
